Borrowed from {{bor|en|hi|तिपाई}}, {{bor|en|ur|تپائی|tr=tipāi|t=teapoy}}, from a merger of {{der|en|sa|त्रिपाद|t=tripod}} + {{der|en|fa-cls|سه پای|tr=sih-pāy|t=tripod}}, with the spelling of the first element influenced by association with {{m|en|tea}}.<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=198386|date=June 2022|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref> {{cog|sa|त्रि|t=three}}, the first element of {{m|sa||त्रिपाद}}, is ultimately derived from {{der|en|ine-pro|*tréyes|t=three}}; while {{cog|fa-cls|پای|tr=pây|t=foot}}, the second element of {{m|fa-cls|سه پای}}, is ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*pṓds|t=foot}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*ped-|t=to step; to walk; to fall; to stumble}}. {{doublet|en|tripod|tripus}}.

